  "id": "three-marginal-coulomb-transport",
  "title": "Three-marginal Coulomb transport",
  "description": "OpenAI's counterexample (2026) to the Monge ansatz: for the Coulomb cost of three particles in space, and every Riesz cost in dimension at least two, a smooth density for which the optimal coupling exists but is given by no pair of maps, although maps come arbitrarily close. A fourth lesson restates the result with infinitesimals: an internal pair of maps at an infinitely fine resolution exceeds the minimum by a positive infinitesimal, and its standard part is the optimal coupling.",
